As a Strategy and Transformation Consultant in our Enterprise Data and Analytics practice, you will help clients turn AI, data, and transformation ambition into practical business value through AI-native consulting that combines strategic thinking with hands-on solution design and delivery.
* Work with emerging AI methods and our frontier partner ecosystem (Microsoft, OpenAI, AWS, Google) to help clients move beyond pilots into enterprise deployment;
* Support engagements across Data & AI strategy, GenAI, agentic AI, governance, and intelligent automation;
* Help identify where AI, analytics, automation, or stronger data foundations can create measurable value;
* Support workshops on AI strategy, use case discovery, prioritization, and AI-ready ways of working;
* Exposure to data strategy, data governance, and modern data foundations, with motivation to learn how these enable scalable AI and analytics;
* Contribute to the design of prototypes, pilots, agents, copilots, workflows, and other implementation-oriented deliverables with multidisciplinary teams;
* Contribute to reusable assets, methods, demos, and offerings that strengthen our AI-native consulting capability;
* Work in a team that values people who build, test, iterate, and make ideas tangible, not only people who create slides.

* 2-4 years of experience in strategy, transformation, data & analytics, AI, digital, or a related field, ideally in consulting, a fast-paced technology environment, or an innovation-driven business role;
* Strong analytical and communication skills, with the ability to connect business priorities and technology implications;
* Hands-on experience with one or more of the following: GenAI, agentic AI, analytics, automation, app builders, workflow orchestration, data products, or AI-enabled transformation initiatives, ideally including experience with n8n, Power Automate, Claude (Chat, Code, Cowork), cloud platforms such as Azure or AWS, and agent frameworks such as LangChain or CrewAI;
* Work with modern AI-native delivery tooling across low-code automation, app building, cloud, and agent orchestration to help make concepts tangible and accelerate prototyping;
* A clear builder mindset: you like turning ideas into something tangible and are comfortable working beyond conceptual advisory;
* Proactive, curious, hands-on, and motivated to learn fast in a frontier environment;
* Fluency in English (written and spoken) is required. German (for Zurich) or French (for Geneva) must be at a business-proficient level (C1).

* Be the change by supporting our clients through innovative strategy projects around digital, future-proof topics that challenge and transform the status quo;
* Craft your own career path through continuous learning and personal growth;
* Experience the benefits of hybrid working, offering flexibility and ensuring work-life balance, 5 weeks of vacation, employee referral bonus, company shares program and annual contribution to a fitness subscription.
Capgemini Switzerland is an equal opportunity employer. We promote equality and dignity in all aspects of recruitment and employment, and all offers of employment and promotions are made on the basis of performance, competence and ability.
Our Capgemini Invent Enterprise Data and Analytics (ED&A) team is at the forefront of helping organizations in Switzerland build robust data foundations for impactful AI, surmounting the -pilot barrier- and scaling innovation.

We empower our clients to unlock the value of data and AI, driving transformation across Life Sciences, Consumer Products and Retail, Financial Services, Manufacturing and Public Sector. If you are passionate about shaping the future of data-driven business, helping organizations in becoming a frontier firm, we want you on our team.
